{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-19981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $u=⟨2,1,-1⟩$ and $v=⟨1,2,0⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-19981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-1))i-(2\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))j+(2\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =2i-j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,u\\times v\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-19981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-19981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-19981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{14}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-19981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{14}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $a=⟨1,0,0⟩$ and $b=⟨0,3,4⟩.$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 3)i-(1\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 0)j+(1\\cdot 3-0\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =0i-4j+3k \\\\  & =⟨0,-4,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-316350" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316350" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-18580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $r=⟨1,-2,3⟩$ and $t=⟨0,1,-2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-18580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\times t & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 1)i-(1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 0)j+(1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,r\\times t\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-18580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-18580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-18580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-18580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-275222" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the triangle spanned by $a=⟨-2,-1,0⟩$ and $b=⟨-4,2,-2⟩.$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-275222" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 0)i-((-2)\\cdot (-2)-(-4)\\cdot 0)j+((-2)\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =2i-4j-8k \\\\  & =⟨2,-4,-8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{2}=\\sqrt{21}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-275222" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-275222" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-275222" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{21}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-275220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $a=⟨-4,-2,1⟩$ and $b=⟨0,-2,-1⟩.$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-275220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 1)i-((-4)\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 1)j+((-4)\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =4i-4j+8k \\\\  & =⟨4,-4,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-275220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-275220" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-275220" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\sqrt{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-127866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the $△\\,ABC,$ if $A(5,0,5),$ $B(6,-1,4),$ $C(9,1,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-127866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(6i-j+4k)-(5i+5k) \\\\  & =i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(9i+j)-(5i+5k) \\\\  & =4i+j-5k \\\\  & =⟨4,1,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-5)-1\\cdot (-1))i-(1\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot (-1))j+(1\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =6i+j+5k \\\\  & =⟨6,1,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{62}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-127866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-127866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-127866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{31}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{31}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{62}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-127866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-127913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the $△\\,PQR,$ if $P(6,1,5),$ $Q(5,1,7),$ $R(4,2,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-127913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(5i+j+7k)-(6i+j+5k) \\\\  & =-i+2k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(4i+2j)-(6i+j+5k) \\\\  & =-2i+j-5k \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot (-5)-1\\cdot 2)i-((-1)\\cdot (-5)-(-2)\\cdot 2)j+((-1)\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =-2i-9j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-9,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-9)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{86}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{86}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-127913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-127913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-127913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\sqrt{13}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{86}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{43}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-127913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{86}}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,LMN$, if $L(-3,0,1)$, $M(0,2,-2)$, $N(2,-1,0).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(2j-2k)-(-3i+k) \\\\  & =3i+2j-3k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(2i-j)-(-3i+k) \\\\  & =5i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨5,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot (-1)-(-3)\\cdot (-1))i-(3\\cdot (-1)-(-3)\\cdot 5)j+(3\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 5)k \\\\  & =-5i-12j-13k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-12,-13⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-12)^{2}+(-13)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+144+169} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{338} \\\\  & =13\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-316363" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316363" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the $△\\,STU,$ if $S(0,1,2),$ $T(2,3,1),$ $U(4,1,2).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SU}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ST} & =t-s \\\\  & =(2i+3j+k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{SU} & =u-s \\\\  & =(4i+j+2k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =4i+0j+0k \\\\  & =⟨4,0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ST}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SU} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 0)i-(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 4)j+(2\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =0i-4j-8k \\\\  & =⟨0,-4,-8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SU}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{ST}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SU}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,STU$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{2}=2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-316530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,PQR$, if $P(1,-2,0)$, $Q(3,1,-1)$, $R(-1,0,2).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(3i+j-k)-(i-2j) \\\\  & =2i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨2,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(-i+2k)-(i-2j) \\\\  & =-2i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2)i-(2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-2))j+(2\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =8i-2j+10k \\\\  & =⟨8,-2,10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+4+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{168} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{42}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{42}}{2}=\\sqrt{42}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-316361" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316361" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{42}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-275225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(-2,0,-1)$, $B(0,-2,-1)$, $C(-3,-2,0).$\n\n$CH=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-275225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2j-k)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =2i-2j \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-3i-2j)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 0)i-(2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)j+(2\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-2i-2j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{44} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{11}}{2}=\\sqrt{11}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ \\sqrt{11} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{11} & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-275225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-275225" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-275225" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-71117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $GH$ of the $△\\,GSM$, if $S(1,-1,2)$, $G(-2,0,2)$, $M(1,1,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-71117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $GH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,GSM$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}GH\\cdot SM\n$$\n\nSo, to find $GH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{SG}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SM}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SG} & =g-s \\\\  & =(-2i+2k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+j \\\\  & =⟨-3,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{SM} & =m-s \\\\  & =(i+j)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SG}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SM} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 0)i-((-3)\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0)j+((-3)\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =-2i-6j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-6,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{SG}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SM}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{SG}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SM}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{76} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,GSM$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{19}}{2}=\\sqrt{19}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $SM$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}SM & =|\\overset{\\to }{SM}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}GH\\cdot SM,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}GH\\cdot SM \\\\ \\sqrt{19} & =\\frac{1}{2}GH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{19} & =GH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ GH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ GH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-71117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-71117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-71117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{19}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{38}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{38}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-71117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-20027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(2,1,2)$, $B(1,2,1)$, $C(3,2,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-20027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(i+2j+k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+2j+3k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-1))i-((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-1))j+((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =2i-2k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-20027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-20027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-20027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-20027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-128013" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $MH$ of the $△\\,LMN,$ if $L(-1,4,1),$ $M(0,3,4),$ $N(1,4,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-128013" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $MH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,LMN$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot LN\n$$\n\nSo, to find $MH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(3j+4k)-(-i+4j+k) \\\\  & =i-j+3k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(i+4j+2k)-(-i+4j+k) \\\\  & =2i+k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 3)i-(1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 3)j+(1\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =-i+5j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $LN$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}LN & =|\\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot LN,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot LN \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot \\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{30} & =MH\\cdot \\sqrt{5} \\\\ MH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ MH & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-128013" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-128013" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-128013" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\sqrt{10}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-128013" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $HK$ of the $△\\,GHI,$ if $G(1,1,1),$ $H(3,2,4),$ $I(2,4,2).$\n\n$HK=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $HK$ can be related to the area of $△\\,GHI$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}HK\\cdot GI\n$$\n\nSo, to find $HK,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{GI}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{GH}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{GI} & =i-g \\\\  & =(2i+4j+2k)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,3,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{GH} & =h-g \\\\  & =(3i+2j+4k)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =2i+j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{GI}\\times \\overset{\\to }{GH} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1)i-(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)j+(1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =8i-j-5k \\\\  & =⟨8,-1,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{GI}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{GH}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{GI}\\times \\overset{\\to }{GH}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,GHI$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $GI$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}GI & =|\\overset{\\to }{GI}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}HK\\cdot GI,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}HK\\cdot \\sqrt{11} \\\\ HK & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\ HK & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{110}}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65eb08de418648285d7b600940653d805ea663f44fdc930793b22e263ee0e271"} {"question" "q-316556" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "q-316556" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\sqrt{110}}{11}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/state.json" "file_sha256" "354efc773f6ebe6b7ddf45851c593c29ac7944010fae67f1ca2a3d7d4b4d525f"} {"question" "e-4344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 4,0,-3 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 5,-1,2 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/example-4344.json" "file_sha256" "be9008b647fd975f0099709ab678151b9570bab88495c7fa68dda2e47757c9b6"} {"question" "e-4344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-1))i-(4\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot 5)j+(4\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 5)k \\\\  & =-3i-23j-4k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-23,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-23)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{554}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\nA_{\\triangle} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{554}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/example-4344.json" "file_sha256" "be9008b647fd975f0099709ab678151b9570bab88495c7fa68dda2e47757c9b6"} {"question" "e-4345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC,$ if $A(1,0,-2),$ $B(-2,0,1),$ $C(1,1,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/example-4345.json" "file_sha256" "a33c2cad52e68b011a7557bbcaa2f942ee343142be1c6db3a33b33cd444e1940"} {"question" "e-4345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j-k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 1)i-(-3\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 0)j+(-3\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =-3i+3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/example-4345.json" "file_sha256" "a33c2cad52e68b011a7557bbcaa2f942ee343142be1c6db3a33b33cd444e1940"} {"question" "e-4346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ if $A(-1,1,0),$ $B(1,1,2),$ $C(1,-1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/example-4346.json" "file_sha256" "af85e9f2cfdc83e3602101d55054860ea26b0101970f16ce6c7d278441a8c628"} {"question" "e-4346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude (height) can be related to the area of the triangle as follows:\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{b \\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding altitude of the triangle.\n\nFor the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC,$ we have $h=CH,$ and $b=AB.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find $A_{\\bigtriangleup}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(i+j+2k)-(-i+j) \\\\  & =2i+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i-j+k)-(-i+j) \\\\  & =2i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-2))i-(2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2)j+(2\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =4i+2j-4k \\\\  & =⟨4,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 6 = 3.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula $A_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/example-4346.json" "file_sha256" "af85e9f2cfdc83e3602101d55054860ea26b0101970f16ce6c7d278441a8c628"}] "usage" {"e-4346" [] "e-4344" [] "q-20027" [] "e-4345" []} "basis" 1406 "retractions" [[17592186106049 :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nCalculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△ABC$, if $A(2, 1, 2)$, $B(1, 2, 1)$, $C(3, 2, 3)$."] [17592186105513 :question/problem "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 4,0,-3 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 5,-1,2 \\rangle$."] [17592186105513 :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 4 & 0 & - 3 \\\\ 5 & - 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}0 & - 3 \\\\ - 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{i} - \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}4 & - 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{j} + \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & - 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = ( 0 \\cdot  2 - ( - 3 ) \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) \\mathbf{i} - ( 4 \\cdot  2 - ( - 3 ) \\cdot  5 ) \\mathbf{j} + ( 4 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) - 0 \\cdot  5 ) \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = - 3 \\mathbf{i} - 23 \\mathbf{j} - 4 \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - 3 , - 23 , - 4 \\rangle  .\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}A & = | \\, \\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} \\, | \\\\  & = \\sqrt{( - 3 {)}^{2} + ( - 23 {)}^{2} + ( - 4 {)}^{2}} \\\\  & = \\sqrt{554} .\\end{array}$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\nA_{\\triangle} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{554}}{2}\n$$"] [17592186105514 :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$, if $A(1,0,-2)$, $B(-2,0,1)$, $C(1,1,-1)$."] [17592186105514 :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\overrightarrow{AB} & = \\mathbf{b} - \\mathbf{a} \\\\  & = ( - 2 \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{k} ) - ( \\mathbf{i} - 2 \\mathbf{k} ) \\\\  & = - 3 \\mathbf{i} + 3 \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - 3 , 0 , 3 \\rangle \\\\ \\overrightarrow{AC} & = \\mathbf{c} - \\mathbf{a} \\\\  & = ( \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{k} ) - ( \\mathbf{i} - 2 \\mathbf{k} ) \\\\  & = \\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  0 , 1 , 1 \\rangle\\end{array}$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\overrightarrow{AB} \\times  \\overrightarrow{AC} & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ - 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{i} - \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{j} + \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = ( 0 \\cdot  1 - 3 \\cdot  1 ) \\mathbf{i} - ( - 3 \\cdot  1 - 3 \\cdot  0 ) \\mathbf{j} + ( - 3 \\cdot  1 - 0 \\cdot  0 ) \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = - 3 \\mathbf{i} + 3 \\mathbf{j} - 3 \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - 3 , 3 , - 3 \\rangle  .\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}A & = | \\overrightarrow{AB} \\times  \\overrightarrow{AC} | \\\\  & = \\sqrt{( - 3 {)}^{2} + {3}^{2} + ( - 3 {)}^{2}} \\\\  & = 3 \\sqrt{3} .\\end{array}$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n$$"] [17592186105515 :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ if $A(-1,1,0)$, $B(1,1,2)$, $C(1,-1,1)$."] [17592186105515 :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH$, we first find $A_{\\bigtriangleup}$. To start, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\overrightarrow{AB} & = \\mathbf{b} - \\mathbf{a} \\\\  & = ( \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j} + 2 \\mathbf{k} ) - ( - \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j} ) \\\\  & = 2 \\mathbf{i} + 2 \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  2 , 0 , 2 \\rangle \\\\ \\overrightarrow{AC} & = \\mathbf{c} - \\mathbf{a} \\\\  & = ( \\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k} ) - ( - \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j} ) \\\\  & = 2 \\mathbf{i} - 2 \\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  2 , - 2 , 1 \\rangle\\end{array}$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\overrightarrow{AB} \\times  \\overrightarrow{AC} & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & - 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}0 & 2 \\\\ - 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{i} - \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{j} + \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & - 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = ( 0 \\cdot  1 - 2 \\cdot  ( - 2 ) ) \\mathbf{i} - ( 2 \\cdot  1 - 2 \\cdot  2 ) \\mathbf{j} + ( 2 \\cdot  ( - 2 ) - 0 \\cdot  2 ) \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = 4 \\mathbf{i} + 2 \\mathbf{j} - 4 \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  4 , 2 , - 4 \\rangle  .\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}A & = | \\overrightarrow{AB} \\times  \\overrightarrow{AC} | \\\\  & = \\sqrt{{4}^{2} + {2}^{2} + ( - 4 {)}^{2}} \\\\  & = \\sqrt{36} \\\\  & = 6.\\end{array}$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 6 = 3\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}A B & = | \\overrightarrow{AB} | \\\\  & = \\sqrt{{2}^{2} + {0}^{2} + {2}^{2}} \\\\  & = \\sqrt{8} \\\\  & = 2 \\sqrt{2}\\end{array}$$\n\nFinally, using the formula\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{△} &= \\frac{1}{2}CH \\cdot AB \\\\\n3 &= \\frac{1}{2}CH \\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\\n3 &= CH \\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\\nCH &= \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\\nCH &= \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186102532 17592186102533 17592186102534 17592186102535 17592186102536] "immutable_fields" [[17592186102531 :answer-field/correct] [17592186102531 :answer-field/id] [17592186102531 :answer-field/key] [17592186102531 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
